# Explicit current607 generic16K updater source option

This is constructed source, not an executed or accepted generic16K updater.
The full accepted-source c6a5de859c3f190d47a5aef30962d2c3b50eaf8d parent is
preserved under parent360/. Its accepted normal/pre86/post87 results are native4K
only. Default source construction reproduces that exact360-file parent.

The explicit generic16k child retains the original607/606 package, transaction,
database preservation, security, dependency-cache, retirement and deadline gates.
It routes the complete parent owner through a pinned owned VM transport and
matches emitted caller, installer, kernel DATA, configuration and policy pins.
Actual current Linux/aarch64/16384-page/kernel facts and current source/run/attempt
guest context are mandatory; Image/config geometry is not a boot result.

Kernel DATA must be supplied as a separate exact three-file immutable source.
There is no automatic historical acquisition. Existing4K fresh/baseline authority
remains a prerequisite and is never promoted to a16K updater outcome.

Native dispatch is through the registered native-arm-build.yml entrypoint, with
explicit page_profile=generic16k, an exact matching source/workflow SHA and a
kernel_input_source publication. All original native input and decision operands
remain required. The enclosing VM transaction remains3900 seconds, including
prepare/QEMU/export; the outer worker remains15600 seconds. Fit is unmeasured.

Source manifests, profile and emitted inverse ledgers are reviewable. No Root
acceptance, physical M2, performance or release credit follows from this source.
New reader binding, native execution and all acceptance decisions belong to Root.
